                    {
                        "sense_id": "4b6f2be7-4847-3964-9e62-42df6845425b",
                        "entry_id": "f1e4268e-4743-3172-92eb-0bae035b408b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Dated spelling of preestablish."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9ae94653-b652-40ac-b9b3-21097999e738",
                                "sense_id": "4b6f2be7-4847-3964-9e62-42df6845425b",
                                "text": "But the future, say they, is necessary, either because the Divinity foresees all things, and even preëstablishes them in governing the universe; or because all things necessarily come to pass by a concatenation of causes."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ad936292-f910-4733-88ba-96c36c09ba31",
                                "sense_id": "4b6f2be7-4847-3964-9e62-42df6845425b",
                                "text": "2. The combination with a plurality of selective devices adapted for use in preëstablishing a signal, of make-and-break devices, one for each of the selecting devices for transmitting said signal and adapted to make slidable contact with the corresponding selective devices at successive periods."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "76e4d0d4-c831-41cc-9e8d-9b6d64516aff",
                                "sense_id": "4b6f2be7-4847-3964-9e62-42df6845425b",
                                "text": "Here we get the Virgil tradition: the monarchy preëstablished by God and founded by Augustus, the descendant of Aeneas, Rome the head of the world through divine ordinance."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
